'''''Astrolepis cochisensis''''' is a species of [[fern]] known by the common name '''Cochise scaly cloak fern'''. It is native to the southwestern United States and northern Mexico, where it occupies mainly desert habitat, often on [[limestone|calcareous soils]].

==Description==
The fern grows from a short [[rhizome]]. The rhizome bears tan scales, sometimes dark at the base, which is up to {{convert|10|mm|in|sigfig=1|sp=us}} long and may or may not have hairlike small teeth on the edge.{{sfn|Windham|1993}} The leaves are {{convert|7|to|40|cm|in|sigfig=2|sp=us}} long, and divided into 20 to 50&nbsp;pairs of [[pinna (botany)|pinna]]e (leaflets) which are sometimes lobed.{{sfn|Windham|1993}} The pinnae are [[Glossary of leaf morphology#oblong|oblong]]. The largest specimens typically measure {{convert|4|to|7|mm|in|sigfig=1|sp=us}} long. Some lack lobes altogether; others bear 1 to 4 lobes, asymmetrically arranged on the pinna. The lobes are broadly rounded, and the indentations between them are shallow.{{sfn|Windham|1993}}

The leaflets are coated in star-shaped scales on the upper surface and hairy lance-shaped scales beneath.

